  "body": "[sigstore/sigstore-conformance](https://github.com/sigstore/sigstore-conformance/) is a conformance test suite that uses  `pytest.main(args)` and the upgrade to pytest 9 broke one of the users:\n* this worked in pytest 8 but not in pytest 9 \n   `args=[\"test/\", ...,  \"--custom-arg\", \"custom/path/here\"]`\n* this works also in pytest 9 \n   `args=[\"test/\", ...,  \"--custom-arg=custom/path/here\"]`\n\n\nThe pytest 9 failure in the first case is an importError from an unexpected import -- it looks like pytest 9 tries to import a conftest.py from the directory structure specified by \"--custom-arg\" so I assume the custom argument value is now considered a test path. \n\nI can see how this might even be a reasonable choice by pytest but figured I'll file an issue in case the change is unintended.  \n\nThese issues seem at least potentially related: #14048, #13913 ",
